  "body": "Part of #2607 (slice S3 of 6).\n\nThe order of the maintainer (2026-11-18): \"GPU shader issues get priority\".\n\n## What\nUse the S2 kernel (#2627) for the viewport playback.\n\n- The kernel writes the `Scene.cut` storage buffer of `crates/ui/src/trace.rs` directly. On the GPU path, the CPU pack and the patch upload (`trace.rs` lines 229 and 236-243) do not run.\n- Keyframes are GPU buffer copies, within a VRAM budget. A seek copies the nearest keyframe and dispatches the remaining moves.\n- Generation runs outside the frame (#2238: frame target under 10 ms).\n- On `DeviceLost` or any error, the CPU playback runs. Log it one time. `CAMCRAFT_GPU_COMPUTE=off` (#2620) turns the GPU path off.\n- Check the wgpu 30 API for a poll with a timeout.\n\n## Tests\n- End-frame parity on the software adapter: the GPU playback picture against the CPU playback picture, within the eye tolerance of `crates/ui/tests/trace_parity.rs`.\n- A fault test: a forced kernel error gives the CPU picture.\n- The `camcraft-ui` lib tests stay green. The `#[test]` count does not go down.\n\n## Prime Directive\nDisplay only. The verdict (`crates/app/src/stock_sim.rs` `simulate_document`) and the post gate do not change.\n\nBlocked by #2627 (S2) and #2611. #2611 is a user bug: the voxel playback shows no visible removal. A parity test against a broken CPU picture has no value.\n\nUI PR: add before and after screenshots to the PR body.\n\nDone means: the viewport playback uses the GPU cut when a device is present, the CPU path runs otherwise, and the parity and fault tests are green.\n",
